WEBVTT

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:16.590
<i>Along a zigzag the world turns,</i>
<i>I heave out a sigh.</i>

00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:27.610
<i>Someone pauses along the way,</i>
<i>but reality moves on.</i>

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:33.140
<i>Treat love as love, treat</i>
<i>dreams as dreams.</i>

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:38.650
<i>It's difficult to say it in earnest.</i>
<i>The times forge ahead, but...</i>

00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:43.620
<i>I want to make you happy...</i>

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:49.420
<i>I'll do so like I do to</i>
<i>be myself. Yeah!</i>

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:54.450
<i>I'll make you happy...</i>

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:59.800
<i>I dedicate all that</i>
<i>I can do to you.</i>

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:11.120
<i>Along a zigzag the world turns,</i>
<i>I heave out a sigh.</i>

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:23.360
<i>Someone pauses along the way,</i>
<i>but love doesn't stop for me.</i>

00:01:35.170 --> 00:01:36.540
"Kitchen"

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:39.780
Hey! This is the manju
I bought last week.

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:41.370
"Hot Springs Manju"
"Manju:" Pastry made of rice and beans.

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:44.440
I wonder if it's still any good?
It's at least a week old.

00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:47.550
It's been kept in the fridge,
so I'm sure it's just fine.

00:01:47.720 --> 00:01:49.950
Really? It won't
be rotten?

00:01:50.390 --> 00:01:55.120
Most souvenir sweets like that
are usually good for a week.

00:01:55.390 --> 00:01:58.120
Yeah, you're right. It even
says so on the box.

00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:01.390
That's good to hear. But we'd
better eat these up today.

00:02:01.570 --> 00:02:04.060
How about passing them around
to everyone this afternoon at 3?

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:05.530
Aha!

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:10.670
FILE. 14
MANJU TERROR!
NATSUMI'S EDO
ESCAPADE

00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:21.280
Yes. Yes, that's
correct.

00:02:27.830 --> 00:02:30.990
I think I'll go make some
tea for everyone.

00:02:35.870 --> 00:02:37.800
What just happened
here?

00:02:37.970 --> 00:02:40.440
Tsujimoto has gone
to make tea?

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:44.430
...10, 11,
12.

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:47.440
12 of these and 9 people at work
today. That leaves 3 left over.

00:02:48.550 --> 00:02:51.710
And tomorrow they'll be no good,
so there's only one thing to do.

00:02:52.450 --> 00:02:55.250
I'm doing this for every-
one's benefit.

00:02:55.350 --> 00:02:59.880
I mean, I wouldn't want anyone
to get sick or anything.

00:02:59.990 --> 00:03:02.150
But these really are
good! Huh?

00:03:02.330 --> 00:03:04.260
Hey, Natsumi. What're
you doing?

00:03:07.670 --> 00:03:10.660
Are you okay,
Natsumi?

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:12.370
Deputy! Deputy! How long
are you planning to sleep?

00:03:12.370 --> 00:03:15.600
"Police"

00:03:15.810 --> 00:03:17.870
Please wake up! There's
a huge problem!

00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:22.640
If you know the base, then you just mul-
tiply by the height and divide by two.

00:03:22.810 --> 00:03:27.250
That's how to find the area of a triangle!
Stop with the nonsense and wake up!

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:28.920
What? What do you want?!

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:32.480
A murdered body's washed up on the riverbank!

00:03:32.590 --> 00:03:34.320
Are you listening
to me? Deputy!

00:03:34.490 --> 00:03:38.090
Get this straight! Just lay
off the bad jokes, okay?

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:39.830
Who are you calling, "Deputy!"

00:03:39.830 --> 00:03:42.260
You certainly look like Deputy Natsumi.

00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:46.230
Huh? What?

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:47.300
No way!

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:49.530
Get with it already...

00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:52.340
...or you'll shame the name of
Deputy Detective Natsumi.

00:03:56.850 --> 00:03:59.750
Where'd these
come from?!

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:14.570
<i>An only woman officer, that's what I am...</i>

00:04:14.570 --> 00:04:18.600
Well, well... Look at that impressive
"maple leaf" mark he left.

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:18.740
<i>An only woman officer, that's what I am...</i>

00:04:18.740 --> 00:04:20.600
What do you think, Deputy?

00:04:20.700 --> 00:04:21.040
<i>... in this rosy City of Edo.</i>

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:25.880
Judging by his calling card, I think we can
assume the killer is a notable hit man.

00:04:25.880 --> 00:04:26.340
<i>... in this rosy City of Edo.</i>

00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:27.380
Yes. The maple leaf on his
cheek is disturbing.

00:04:27.380 --> 00:04:30.580
<i>Hate the crime, not the criminal...</i>

00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:30.950
However, if this is the
work of a hit man...

00:04:30.950 --> 00:04:33.220
<i>I look at the sky, there goes another day.</i>

00:04:33.220 --> 00:04:34.390
...you would expect the victim
to be a high-ranking criminal.

00:04:34.390 --> 00:04:35.390
<i>Sometimes you can't show yourtears...</i>

00:04:35.390 --> 00:04:38.390
But this guy is just a punk.

00:04:38.390 --> 00:04:40.760
And according to a woman who claims
to have seen the perpetrator...
<i>Sometimes you can't show yourtears...</i>

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:41.460
<i>O'my cherry blossom...</i>

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:43.960
...something was said about "hot springs."

00:04:43.960 --> 00:04:45.100
<i>O'my cherry blossom...</i>

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:47.360
I heard that, too. Deputy Natsumi...

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:48.070
<i>... cries on my back!</i>

00:04:48.070 --> 00:04:50.600
Go into town and interview the woman.

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:53.200
Yes, sir. Her name's Futaba, she
lives in the Shosuke tenements.

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:56.200
But she said she couldn't
see the perp's face.

00:04:56.370 --> 00:05:01.000
Make sure that nobody silences
her before she can talk.

00:05:01.180 --> 00:05:06.170
Rest assured. I know the Futabas.
I will make sure that she is safe.

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:09.210
What'd I go and
say that for?

00:05:09.390 --> 00:05:15.020
Anyway, what secret's so important that
people have to be killed over it?

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:19.260
We don't know, that's why we're
having such a hard time.

00:05:19.830 --> 00:05:21.890
A maple leaf and
hot springs...

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:23.930
A maple leaf and hot springs, huh?

00:05:23.930 --> 00:05:25.960
What do you think of hot springs in autumn?

00:05:26.070 --> 00:05:28.330
Get in the water, have
a little hot sake...

00:05:28.540 --> 00:05:31.510
Silence, fool! What does that
have to do with the murder?

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:33.010
Sorry, Deputy.

00:05:33.010 --> 00:05:34.650
Unbelievable!

00:05:34.650 --> 00:05:37.670
Coming through! Outta my way!

00:05:38.920 --> 00:05:40.380
That's dangerous, lady!

00:05:40.380 --> 00:05:44.410
If we had shackles, I'd catch her and tie her up!

00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:48.390
My, my!

00:05:56.170 --> 00:05:57.430
Oh.

00:05:57.430 --> 00:05:59.370
Dr. Kobayakawa!

00:05:59.470 --> 00:06:01.530
Hello! Beautiful
day, isn't it?

00:06:01.710 --> 00:06:02.610
Hello.

00:06:02.610 --> 00:06:04.700
Hello.
Where are you off to today?

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:06.540
On a house call.

00:06:06.540 --> 00:06:10.070
On a house call.
I suppose you would be, being a doctor and all.

00:06:10.250 --> 00:06:12.980
Please forgive him. He's a little
rough around the edges.

00:06:13.150 --> 00:06:14.380
Not at all.

00:06:14.820 --> 00:06:19.020
It's good that you detectives
have so much enthusiasm.

00:06:19.190 --> 00:06:20.320
That's very kind of...

00:06:20.320 --> 00:06:23.380
Yes! You're certainly right there! I'm
so happy I have energy to burn!

00:06:23.560 --> 00:06:26.000
By the way, who are you
paying a house call on?

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:29.890
To Mr. Futaba, of the Shosuke
tenements.

00:06:30.100 --> 00:06:32.430
What luck! I mean, uh,
what a coincidence.

00:06:32.540 --> 00:06:35.160
That's precisely where
we're headed!

00:06:35.270 --> 00:06:39.140
Well let's go there together! Let's go!
Let's go right now!

00:06:39.310 --> 00:06:40.240
Hey!

00:06:40.240 --> 00:06:42.250
Allow me to carry your things.

00:06:42.250 --> 00:06:43.870
It's fine, really.

00:06:44.050 --> 00:06:47.180
Is he a total
doofus?

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:49.180
"Umbrellas"

00:06:50.590 --> 00:06:52.420
How does it look, Doctor?

00:06:52.420 --> 00:06:56.760
It seems much better. Still, you should
refrain from working a little longer.

00:06:56.930 --> 00:06:58.660
I understand.

00:06:58.660 --> 00:06:59.730
Okay. On your side.

00:06:59.730 --> 00:07:00.790
Right.

00:07:00.900 --> 00:07:03.870
Lucky guy. I wish I was sick, too!

00:07:04.030 --> 00:07:06.370
There's no medicine
to cure idiots.

00:07:06.470 --> 00:07:07.870
Excuse me, Miss Futaba.

00:07:07.870 --> 00:07:08.610
Yes?

00:07:08.610 --> 00:07:10.470
I've heard that you saw the murderer.

00:07:10.640 --> 00:07:13.540
Would you describe the incident
to me once again?

00:07:13.710 --> 00:07:18.710
Certainly. That night, I'd just gone to
make a delivery to a good client.

00:07:19.180 --> 00:07:21.810
It was quite late
at night, and...

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:27.920
...I was worried about Father, so I thought
I'd take a short cut along the riverbank.

00:07:29.430 --> 00:07:32.760
<i>"...that hot spring!"</i>

00:07:40.670 --> 00:07:42.610
<i>"Is someone</i>
<i>out there?"</i>

00:07:44.040 --> 00:07:47.840
And without a word, he
ran off like the wind.

00:07:49.610 --> 00:07:52.050
I'm afraid that's all
I can remember.

00:07:52.220 --> 00:07:55.880
So the perpetrator must
be very agile.

00:07:56.290 --> 00:07:58.260
Does it sound like the murderer?

00:07:58.260 --> 00:08:00.220
We can't be sure about that.

00:08:00.390 --> 00:08:04.420
It seems that the perpetrator wants
us to believe he's a hit man.

00:08:04.930 --> 00:08:06.800
Lots of questions to be answered.

00:08:06.800 --> 00:08:07.970
Doctor?

00:08:07.970 --> 00:08:09.690
Yes, that's all for today.

00:08:09.830 --> 00:08:12.890
Doctor, sorry to trouble
you with a house call.

00:08:13.070 --> 00:08:18.100
No need to apologize. Making house calls
is just part of the job.

00:08:18.280 --> 00:08:19.240
Doctor.

00:08:19.240 --> 00:08:20.010
Yes?

00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:22.980
Please take what I have.
It's not much, I'm afraid.

00:08:23.150 --> 00:08:26.080
Nevermind, Miss Futaba.
Put it away.

00:08:26.250 --> 00:08:27.020
But...

00:08:27.020 --> 00:08:30.890
Use it to buy healthy food for your father.

00:08:30.890 --> 00:08:32.880
Thank you.

00:08:33.060 --> 00:08:35.530
I'll be back again.

00:08:41.630 --> 00:08:42.800
I love windmills!

00:08:42.800 --> 00:08:44.730
Hey, wait up!

00:08:44.900 --> 00:08:48.030
You're very admirable,
Dr. Kobayakawa!

00:08:48.210 --> 00:08:50.170
Please, you're embar-
rassing me.

00:08:50.610 --> 00:08:53.470
It's nothing compared to
your kindness, Deputy.

00:08:53.580 --> 00:08:54.870
It's well-known that because
of you two...

00:08:54.980 --> 00:08:58.810
...people can go about their business and
not have to worry about their safety.

00:08:58.980 --> 00:09:01.950
Enough, Doctor. All this flattery
will go straight to my head.

00:09:02.220 --> 00:09:04.190
I speak the
truth!

00:09:07.190 --> 00:09:09.350
Why hello,
little kitty!

00:09:09.530 --> 00:09:11.730
"Oniichan:" an older brother, or brother figure
Oniichan!

00:09:11.730 --> 00:09:13.700
Look here!
It's Maho!

00:09:13.860 --> 00:09:17.030
Thank you for the
bear stuffed doll!

00:09:17.230 --> 00:09:20.260
What do you know! So this
is where you live, is it?

00:09:20.440 --> 00:09:21.370
Mm-hmm.

00:09:21.540 --> 00:09:23.510
So, what are you
up to today?

00:09:23.670 --> 00:09:25.670
Here, this is
for you!

00:09:25.840 --> 00:09:26.570
Wow.

00:09:26.740 --> 00:09:29.740
I learned how to make it at school,
and it works good, too!

00:09:29.910 --> 00:09:32.640
Sure I can
have it?

00:09:32.820 --> 00:09:35.880
I made it so I could
give it to you.

00:09:36.050 --> 00:09:38.750
Really? Well then,
I can't say no.

00:09:38.860 --> 00:09:39.980
Thank you very
much.

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:41.320
Okay!

00:09:41.490 --> 00:09:44.260
I'll put it right in here,
so I don't lose it.

00:09:44.430 --> 00:09:45.660
Okay!

00:09:45.830 --> 00:09:51.230
Somebody's got a lot of time on his
hands... playing with children.

00:10:00.680 --> 00:10:01.980
Here you are.

00:10:01.980 --> 00:10:05.480
Here you are.
Thank you very much for your patronage.

00:10:05.480 --> 00:10:05.620
Thank you very much for your patronage.

00:10:05.620 --> 00:10:07.620
Thank you. See you again.

00:10:07.620 --> 00:10:10.090
Good night.

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:14.090
Very good. I'll be able to
pay Dr. Miyuki now.

00:10:14.320 --> 00:10:16.090
"Kobayakawa"
"For all illnesses"

00:10:17.030 --> 00:10:20.260
That's strange. It's
always left open.

00:10:20.630 --> 00:10:22.660
Hello? Are you
in, Doctor?

00:10:25.200 --> 00:10:28.140
Doctor? Are
you in?

00:10:28.240 --> 00:10:31.000
It's Futaba. Hmm?

00:10:34.750 --> 00:10:38.040
I'm sure that building
used to be vacant.

00:10:38.680 --> 00:10:41.340
What's with all
that steam?

00:10:41.450 --> 00:10:43.580
Doctor! What
on earth?!

00:11:00.900 --> 00:11:04.030
Stabbed right through the heart!
What a cruel deed!

00:11:04.440 --> 00:11:07.970
It looks like the work of
the same murderer.

00:11:08.150 --> 00:11:08.980
Yeah.

00:11:09.150 --> 00:11:13.380
Apparently he was going to the doctor
to pay for his medical treatment.

00:11:13.550 --> 00:11:16.080
That's how he ended
up here.

00:11:16.750 --> 00:11:17.450
"Manji?"

00:11:17.620 --> 00:11:18.850
What's "manji?"

00:11:19.020 --> 00:11:22.890
First we have maple leaves and hot
springs. And now this "manji."

00:11:22.990 --> 00:11:26.220
This is getting more confusing all the
time. Are there any other clues?

00:11:26.660 --> 00:11:30.290
Other than him collecting funds from
his customers, there's nothing...

00:11:30.470 --> 00:11:35.460
Considering that the money wasn't taken,
it doesn't look like a robbery.

00:11:35.640 --> 00:11:40.510
So in other words, we're dealing
with a serial killer.

00:11:40.680 --> 00:11:42.300
Father!

00:11:42.410 --> 00:11:44.310
Let me pass! Please
let me pass!

00:11:44.480 --> 00:11:45.620
I cannot let you.

00:11:45.620 --> 00:11:46.780
I cannot let you.
Father!

00:11:46.950 --> 00:11:49.980
Miss Futaba. Compose yourself.
You must be strong.

00:11:51.620 --> 00:11:52.950
Poor young
lady.

00:11:53.120 --> 00:11:58.080
Just when it looked as though
he was going to recover.

00:11:58.200 --> 00:12:00.720
Apparently he had
many debts.

00:12:00.900 --> 00:12:03.530
We should all give our support
to Miss Futaba.

00:12:03.630 --> 00:12:06.600
Deputy, I know this may be difficult
for you, but this is work.

00:12:06.700 --> 00:12:08.930
I'm going to question
the Doctor.

00:12:09.110 --> 00:12:11.070
Yes.

00:12:11.840 --> 00:12:14.870
Last night I received an
unexpected call...

00:12:14.980 --> 00:12:18.910
...and by the time I returned
home, it was very late.

00:12:19.020 --> 00:12:23.580
Because it was dark, I didn't see Futaba's
body lying on the ground.

00:12:23.750 --> 00:12:27.990
When I think that if only I'd seen him,
I might've been able to save him...

00:12:28.160 --> 00:12:30.180
...I am filled with
remorse.

00:12:30.360 --> 00:12:32.390
Doctor!

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:37.870
By the way, Doctor. I must ask you where
you claim to have gone last night.

00:12:38.370 --> 00:12:40.140
Pardon? Are you saying...

00:12:40.140 --> 00:12:43.570
Pardon? Are you saying...
If you can't prove you were not at home when...

00:12:43.670 --> 00:12:47.040
...Futaba was killed, then
you don't have an alibi.

00:12:48.050 --> 00:12:50.550
Sheriff! No!

00:12:50.550 --> 00:12:51.740
No.

00:12:51.850 --> 00:12:54.610
It'd be hard for someone to duplicate the
intricacy of this murderer's handiwork.

00:12:54.720 --> 00:12:57.050
I'd just like her to tell
us, for the record.

00:12:57.220 --> 00:12:59.850
I'll take you
there.

00:13:00.020 --> 00:13:01.330
We'll go with her.

00:13:01.330 --> 00:13:02.630
Please do.

00:13:02.630 --> 00:13:04.590
Let's go.

00:13:11.700 --> 00:13:16.200
We'll need to thoroughly
investigate the Doctor.

00:13:16.370 --> 00:13:18.340
Sheriff!

00:13:24.720 --> 00:13:25.980
Father...

00:13:25.980 --> 00:13:28.420
Oh! Look what we have here.

00:13:28.590 --> 00:13:32.520
Trying to make your debts just wash
away, like your Father's spirit?!

00:13:33.020 --> 00:13:34.650
No, I'm not.

00:13:34.760 --> 00:13:37.420
Right after his funeral, I'll
repay what he owes you.

00:13:37.590 --> 00:13:38.800
Well, that'll take too long...

00:13:38.800 --> 00:13:41.530
Meanwhile, gimme some interest!

00:13:41.530 --> 00:13:42.130
Yeah!

00:13:42.130 --> 00:13:44.230
Aah! Stop it!

00:13:44.400 --> 00:13:44.500
Stop it! Please!

00:13:44.500 --> 00:13:46.770
We'll get you into good form!

00:13:46.940 --> 00:13:47.490
Come here!

00:13:47.670 --> 00:13:51.110
Don't! Please
stop!

00:13:59.120 --> 00:14:01.080
Get me outta here!
Get me outta here!

00:14:05.920 --> 00:14:07.720
Oh, no!

00:14:17.170 --> 00:14:19.660
Let's not go through
with this.

00:14:19.840 --> 00:14:23.270
There's no room in our business
for compassion. Think about it.

00:14:23.370 --> 00:14:27.070
A beautiful woman like her, living alone.
And she has no interest in men.

00:14:27.180 --> 00:14:29.170
That, in itself, is
an enigma.

00:14:29.350 --> 00:14:31.080
That's the silliest thing
I've ever heard.

00:14:31.250 --> 00:14:35.340
Anyway, we won't know a thing unless
we go and investigate. Come on.

00:14:35.520 --> 00:14:37.850
Maybe he's just
a voyeur.

00:14:43.430 --> 00:14:45.230
What? Doesn't look like she's here.

00:14:45.230 --> 00:14:47.160
Just what were you hoping for, anyway?

00:14:47.330 --> 00:14:50.270
Uh... nothing in particular.
What's that over there?

00:14:51.170 --> 00:14:53.400
It's a bath!

00:14:53.400 --> 00:14:55.870
I'll definitely have to check that out!

00:14:56.040 --> 00:14:58.440
No! Don't!

00:15:05.880 --> 00:15:09.110
Wow! Come here! Hurry!
Take a look at this!

00:15:15.060 --> 00:15:17.820
Why? Why
me?

00:15:32.240 --> 00:15:32.510
"Sake"

00:15:32.510 --> 00:15:35.570
Anyway, it appears that
they've been drinking.
"Sake"

00:15:35.570 --> 00:15:35.580
"Sake"

00:15:40.280 --> 00:15:41.880
Oh! Deputy
Natsumi.

00:15:42.750 --> 00:15:43.490
Sheriff Tokuno.

00:15:43.490 --> 00:15:45.610
You're here from the south?

00:15:45.860 --> 00:15:48.720
When a thing like this can
happen to our officers...

00:15:48.830 --> 00:15:51.730
...the barriers between north
and south disappear.

00:15:51.830 --> 00:15:53.230
Take a look at this.

00:15:53.230 --> 00:15:54.490
Take a look at this.
Yes!

00:15:54.660 --> 00:15:58.430
What a disgrace. To think the sheriff
himself would get offed.

00:15:59.140 --> 00:16:02.040
The perpetrator
is very skilled.

00:16:02.140 --> 00:16:03.900
Death is almost always
instantaneous.

00:16:04.070 --> 00:16:09.810
"Manji..." To have it happen at a temple...
Maybe that's what Futaba is telling us.

00:16:10.250 --> 00:16:13.740
No, the murderer probably
did that.

00:16:13.850 --> 00:16:17.720
From the positions of the bodies, I'd say
they were carried here from elsewhere.

00:16:17.820 --> 00:16:20.550
But what's with this red
and white cloth?

00:16:20.720 --> 00:16:23.250
Hmm. This is
a real puzzle.

00:16:23.430 --> 00:16:26.290
What we need to do is go back to the
start and rethink the entire case.

00:16:29.200 --> 00:16:33.640
A maple leaf, a hot spring, a red
and white cloth, and "manji."

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:37.540
I'm certain that these things
are leading to something.

00:16:38.040 --> 00:16:42.410
Once we know what that is, we'll
know the murderer's motive.

00:16:42.580 --> 00:16:45.140
That reminds me, yesterday,
the sheriff said...

00:16:45.250 --> 00:16:48.810
...that he was going to pay
a visit to Dr. Kobayakawa.

00:16:49.320 --> 00:16:50.320
Wh... What?

00:16:50.320 --> 00:16:53.150
Wh... What?
Then she's under even more suspicion.

00:16:53.620 --> 00:16:56.150
But she's a good
person.

00:16:56.260 --> 00:17:00.200
A person who saves lives wouldn't
go around murdering people!

00:17:00.430 --> 00:17:01.800
But a perpetrator...

00:17:01.800 --> 00:17:02.630
No! You're wrong!

00:17:02.630 --> 00:17:03.470
What?

00:17:03.470 --> 00:17:06.130
The Doctor is not a criminal!

00:17:06.300 --> 00:17:07.860
I'll go and
prove it!

00:17:08.040 --> 00:17:09.070
Prove it?

00:17:09.070 --> 00:17:09.910
How?

00:17:09.910 --> 00:17:12.930
I'll ask her in person! So, here I go!

00:17:13.110 --> 00:17:14.510
Wait! Let's talk about it...

00:17:14.510 --> 00:17:15.780
Deputy!

00:17:15.780 --> 00:17:15.910
Ooph!

00:17:15.910 --> 00:17:17.470
My cart has been stolen!

00:17:17.580 --> 00:17:20.570
Help me find it! If I don't have my
cart, I can't go to the market!

00:17:20.750 --> 00:17:22.350
But... but I...

00:17:22.350 --> 00:17:26.410
Forget him and help me!

00:17:31.230 --> 00:17:33.460
Doctor? Where are
you, Doctor?

00:17:33.830 --> 00:17:37.430
I have to speak
with you. Oh?

00:17:39.670 --> 00:17:41.070
"Sheriff"

00:17:42.240 --> 00:17:45.040
These are the Sheriff's
sandals.

00:17:45.210 --> 00:17:48.180
So that means that he did
come here after all!

00:17:49.310 --> 00:17:53.510
Huh?! What's
going on?!

00:17:54.050 --> 00:17:56.580
This is amazing!

00:17:56.790 --> 00:17:58.550
It's all manju!

00:17:58.890 --> 00:18:01.260
Hot springs manju,
maple leaf manju...

00:18:01.360 --> 00:18:04.050
...red and white manju,
and sake manju!

00:18:04.160 --> 00:18:05.920
The victims...

00:18:07.200 --> 00:18:11.930
...this is what they were
trying to tell us.

00:18:16.340 --> 00:18:18.310
I'm choking!

00:18:36.390 --> 00:18:37.260
Deputy!

00:18:37.260 --> 00:18:43.130
I don't believe it! I was the
perpetrator all along. It can't be!

00:18:43.300 --> 00:18:46.200
So you've finally become
yourself again.

00:18:46.300 --> 00:18:50.260
Without even knowing it, you were
coming here every night.

00:18:50.370 --> 00:18:51.510
Do you remember anything?

00:18:51.510 --> 00:18:52.910
No, nothing.

00:18:52.910 --> 00:18:55.780
How?! How could you do this to me?!

00:18:55.950 --> 00:18:58.510
I don't know.
Only...

00:18:58.680 --> 00:19:01.240
...only that I had to
keep it a secret.

00:19:01.420 --> 00:19:03.980
And the secret was
this manju house.

00:19:04.550 --> 00:19:06.580
Yes.

00:19:06.690 --> 00:19:09.990
I had to keep it a secret. I couldn't let
anyone find out about this place.

00:19:10.430 --> 00:19:12.690
And the pressure of keeping
that secret...

00:19:12.800 --> 00:19:15.560
...induced a split personality
disorder.

00:19:16.200 --> 00:19:19.360
When the law enforcer part
of you was sleeping...

00:19:19.470 --> 00:19:24.030
...another self would arise. And
then you would come here.

00:19:24.610 --> 00:19:27.700
Without telling anyone, you'd just come
and make hundreds of manju.

00:19:28.040 --> 00:19:31.210
You coveted the manju as
if you were possessed.

00:19:31.750 --> 00:19:34.650
Your conscious mind wouldn't know.

00:19:34.650 --> 00:19:38.610
Your conscious mind wouldn't know.
No... no. But why?! Why would I do this?!

00:19:39.090 --> 00:19:39.860
The reason...

00:19:39.860 --> 00:19:40.850
Yes? What?

00:19:41.020 --> 00:19:44.620
The reason is something you should
know better than anyone, Natsumi.

00:19:44.890 --> 00:19:47.520
Who, me? But
I don't.

00:19:47.630 --> 00:19:50.570
Tell me, Doctor! Please!
Tell me!

00:19:50.730 --> 00:19:56.040
Think back and remember. Right
back to the beginning.

00:19:56.040 --> 00:19:58.560
Don't you deny it, Tsujimoto.

00:19:58.740 --> 00:19:59.740
Waah!

00:19:59.740 --> 00:20:01.640
We all know.

00:20:01.640 --> 00:20:02.470
Know what?

00:20:02.650 --> 00:20:06.050
About you and manju.
We know everything.

00:20:07.850 --> 00:20:10.820
Now everybody's
found out.

00:20:11.520 --> 00:20:13.510
Why don't you
give it up?

00:20:13.960 --> 00:20:15.980
We'll forgive you
if you apologize.

00:20:16.160 --> 00:20:17.760
A grudge against gluttony...

00:20:17.760 --> 00:20:19.520
...is pure terror.

00:20:20.260 --> 00:20:22.930
What are you all saying? What
do you want me to do?

00:20:23.500 --> 00:20:23.670
Hot springs manju!

00:20:23.670 --> 00:20:25.690
What am I supposed to do?

00:20:25.870 --> 00:20:27.300
She's still denying it.

00:20:27.300 --> 00:20:28.640
What a terrible person.

00:20:28.640 --> 00:20:30.300
Give us an apology!

00:20:34.840 --> 00:20:36.210
Natsumi!

00:20:36.310 --> 00:20:38.280
Hey! Wake up!

00:20:38.380 --> 00:20:41.370
Hey, Natsumi!
Natsumi!

00:20:41.550 --> 00:20:44.450
The terror of manju...

00:20:45.690 --> 00:20:48.620
Are you okay,
Natsumi?!

00:20:49.090 --> 00:20:50.960
No! Don't
kill me!

00:20:51.130 --> 00:20:53.300
What's wrong with you?

00:20:53.300 --> 00:20:55.360
What's wrong with you?
Are you okay?

00:20:55.800 --> 00:20:58.630
Do you remember slipping and
hitting your head on the floor?

00:20:59.270 --> 00:21:03.170
You mean... you mean everything
up until now was just?

00:21:03.270 --> 00:21:09.110
Thank goodness! Sorry to
have troubled all of you.

00:21:11.010 --> 00:21:13.380
Now that you're feeling more like yourself,
there's something we'd like to ask you.

00:21:13.550 --> 00:21:14.810
Which is?

00:21:14.980 --> 00:21:17.780
Tell us, what is the meaning of
this, Natsumi Tsujimoto?!

00:21:18.720 --> 00:21:19.380
Uh-oh!

00:21:19.560 --> 00:21:21.960
We were supposed to
share it, remember?

00:21:22.130 --> 00:21:24.620
I thought something was up when you
offered to make tea for everyone.

00:21:24.790 --> 00:21:27.730
Of course you didn't sit here and eat
them all by yourself, did you?

00:21:27.900 --> 00:21:30.920
Oh, that...
I can...

00:21:31.100 --> 00:21:33.070
I guess I've been caught
red-handed.

00:21:39.140 --> 00:21:40.540
I'm really and truly sorry!

00:21:40.540 --> 00:21:41.670
I won't forgive you.

00:21:41.780 --> 00:21:42.510
Oh, Natsumi!

00:21:42.510 --> 00:21:43.550
You're not going to get away with this!

00:21:43.550 --> 00:21:46.140
Don't expect me to let you off easy!

00:21:46.320 --> 00:21:51.020
Don't get steamed
about the manju!

00:22:02.400 --> 00:22:10.970
<i>I live my life my own way, doing</i>
<i>things others wouldn't.</i>

00:22:11.240 --> 00:22:19.580
<i>Being strong isn't enough.</i>
<i>It makes me lonely.</i>

00:22:22.290 --> 00:22:30.590
<i>I can feel your presence</i>
<i>as if you're right here...</i>

00:22:31.130 --> 00:22:38.700
<i>... but I can't say a word.</i>

00:22:40.240 --> 00:22:47.500
<i>The feelings I hide within might</i>
<i>break into pieces...</i>

00:22:49.050 --> 00:22:56.420
<i>But if I don't say anything,</i>
<i>nothing can begin.</i>

00:22:56.750 --> 00:23:03.920
<i>The wind gently blows...</i>
<i>Time flows...</i>

00:23:04.090 --> 00:23:13.640
<i>Time flows... And soon</i>
<i>I can be honest...</i>

00:23:13.770 --> 00:23:16.740
<i>Thank you,</i>
<i>friend!</i>

00:23:23.150 --> 00:23:24.940
"Woman Without Luck"

00:23:26.580 --> 00:23:28.310
Oh, not again! She's back!

00:23:28.480 --> 00:23:31.080
This time it's a survival game.

00:23:31.250 --> 00:23:32.590
Yoriko, you have to do something.

00:23:32.760 --> 00:23:34.380
Hey, I'm the victim here.

00:23:34.560 --> 00:23:36.460
You shouldn't get us involved.

00:23:36.630 --> 00:23:38.620
That's true. Come on...

00:23:38.800 --> 00:23:41.130
I think both of you
are enjoying this.

00:23:41.300 --> 00:23:43.460
What?

00:23:43.630 --> 00:23:45.730
Next time, You're Under
Arrest, File 15...

00:23:45.840 --> 00:23:47.840
"Up Against Chie Sagami-
Ono... Again!"

00:23:47.970 --> 00:23:49.970
Who will be the
sole survivor?
